From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 22:16:15 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] users: Offer fingerprint login when GDM is not installed

The Fingerprint Login row only appeared when GDM's org.gnome.login-screen
schema was installed and enable-fingerprint-authentication was set. On a
system without GDM -- Phosh on a phone, whose lock screen unlocks with a
fingerprint through fprintd -- the schema does not exist, so a user with
a working reader had no way to enrol a finger at all.

Keep deferring to GDM's setting when it exists, and treat its absence as
no policy against it.

Rebased onto 51.0, which rewrote this condition: it dropped the
act_user_is_local_account() term and reflowed the expression, so the
50.4 patch no longer applied.

Assisted-by: Claude
Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
 panels/system/users/cc-user-page.c | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/panels/system/users/cc-user-page.c
+++ b/panels/system/users/cc-user-page.c
@@ -344,9 +344,11 @@
     CcFingerprintState state = cc_fingerprint_manager_get_state (manager);
     gboolean visible = FALSE;
 
+    /* Without GDM there is no login-screen policy to defer to; the lock
+     * screen (Phosh's, for one) can still take a fingerprint. */
     visible = (act_user_get_uid (self->user) == getuid ()
-               && (self->login_screen_settings
-                   && g_settings_get_boolean (self->login_screen_settings, "enable-fingerprint-authentication")));
+               && (!self->login_screen_settings
+                   || g_settings_get_boolean (self->login_screen_settings, "enable-fingerprint-authentication")));
     gtk_widget_set_visible (GTK_WIDGET (self->fingerprint_row), visible);
     if (!visible)
         return;
